Campus operation has no traffic lights and the vehicle carries no camera into this
pipeline, yet the two traffic_light containers still ran at 47% CPU each. Turning the
module off measured: load 29.4 -> 20.6, RViz 3 -> 5 fps, and obstacle_segmentation
recovered from publishing nothing to 2.147 Hz (it had been starved of CPU). The whole
traffic-light subtree - arbiter, crosswalk_estimator, map_based_detector,
multi_camera_fusion - drops to zero nodes, with no process deaths.

use_traffic_light_recognition is not exposed through autoware.launch.xml or
logging_simulator.launch.xml, so the default in the component launch file is the only
place to change it. Re-enable by passing use_traffic_light_recognition:=true if a
camera-equipped route ever needs it.

--- a/autoware_launch/launch/components/tier4_perception_component.launch.xml
+++ b/autoware_launch/launch/components/tier4_perception_component.launch.xml
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
   <arg name="use_roi_detected_object_validator" default="true" description="if true, detected objects are validated by ROI and camera-lidar fusion results are filtered accordingly"/>
   <arg name="use_semantic_segmentation_ptv3" default="false" description="use semantic segmentation ptv3 for ground segmentation"/>
   <arg name="use_empty_dynamic_object_publisher" default="false" description="if true, /perception/object_recognition/objects topic has an empty DynamicObjectArray"/>
-  <arg name="use_traffic_light_recognition" default="true" description="use traffic light recognition module, if false, traffic light recognition module will not be launched"/>
+  <arg name="use_traffic_light_recognition" default="false" description="use traffic light recognition module, if false, traffic light recognition module will not be launched"/>
 
   <arg name="use_low_height_cropbox" default="false" description="use low height crop filter in clustering"/>
   <arg name="use_vector_map" default="true" description="use vector map in prediction"/>
